# 1. A server suddenly becomes slow. How will you troubleshoot it?

"First, I will check CPU usage using top or htop. Then I will check memory usage using free -h and disk usage using df -h. I will check which processes are consuming high resources. After that, I will check application and system logs using tail or journalctl. I will also check network connectivity if required. Finally, I will identify the root cause, fix it, and monitor the server to make sure the performance is normal."
