Linux commands knowledge (top, htop, ps)
Root cause analysis
Monitoring and problem-solving skills

> Short Answer (Interview Friendly):
"I will check high CPU-consuming processes using top or htop, analyze logs, identify the root cause, take corrective action such as restarting services or scaling resources, and continuously monitor the system."


# 3. Memory utilization is continuously increasing. What will you do?
Answer:
"First, I will verify memory usage using commands like free -h, top, htop, or vmstat. Then I will identify which process is consuming excessive memory. I will check application logs and monitor the process over time to determine whether there is a memory leak, excessive caching, or an abnormal workload. Based on the findings, I may restart the affected service, optimize the application, clear unnecessary cache, or increase resources if required. Finally, I will continue monitoring to ensure memory usage stabilizes."

