# 4. Disk utilization has reached 100%. How will you recover the server?
Answer:
"First, I will check disk usage using commands like df -h and identify which filesystem is full. Then I will use du -sh to find large files and directories consuming space. I will check logs, temporary files, old backups, and unnecessary data that can be safely removed. If a deleted file is still held open by a process, I will identify it using lsof and restart the process if required. I may also archive old data, extend the disk volume, or add additional storage if needed. Finally, I will monitor disk usage and set up alerts to prevent future issues."

