Disk management knowledge
Commands like df, du, lsof
Root cause analysis and recovery approach

> Short Answer (Interview Friendly):
"I will use df -h and du -sh to identify disk usage, remove unnecessary files, check for deleted but open files using lsof, free up space, and monitor the server to avoid future disk-full issues."


# 5. SSH is not working. How do you troubleshoot?
Answer:
"First, I will check whether the server is reachable using ping or network connectivity tests. Then I will verify that the SSH service is running using systemctl status sshd (or ssh). I will check if port 22 is listening using netstat or ss, and verify firewall and security group rules. Next, I will review SSH logs (/var/log/auth.log or /var/log/secure) for authentication or configuration errors. If needed, I will restart the SSH service and validate the SSH configuration. Finally, I will test the connection again and monitor for any further issues."

