# 6. A service is failing after every reboot. What will you check?
Answer:
"First, I will check the service status using systemctl status <service>. Then I will check the service logs using journalctl -u <service> to identify the error. I will verify whether the service is enabled to start automatically using systemctl is-enabled <service>. I will also check service dependencies, configuration files, required ports, permissions, and whether the required network or database services are available after reboot. Finally, I will fix the root cause, enable the service if required, restart it, and verify that it starts successfully after another reboot."

Hindi me Question ka matlab:
"Agar server reboot karne ke baad koi service baar-baar fail ho jaati hai, to aap kya check karoge?"

Interviewer kya dekhna chahta hai?

systemctl knowledge
Log checking
Service dependencies
Boot/startup configuration
Root cause analysis

Short Answer (Interview Friendly):

"I will check the service status and logs, verify whether it is enabled at boot, check dependencies and configuration, fix the root cause, and test the service after reboot."


